b:
As a magician, I can't tell *how* because it would be unethical, but I can give some insight:

- They are regular cubes with an extra something;

- A skilled cuber would catch on what's added to them INSTANTLY but only by picking up both cubes;

- It costs good money (roughly 400 usd) to learn this and obtain the special materials, which can only be sourced from a single person - the creator of this miracle;

- There *is* sleight of hand involved;

- A regular cuber who's not a magician can hardly pull off the same effect because there is far more showmanship there than you would think and THAT is a major part of how and *why* it works. 

Any further detailing would probably spoil unwanted stuff. If you're interested in cube magic I recommend a well-known magician's Cube3 to get you started. 

I urge anyone who may know the stuff I talked about earlier in this post to NOT spoil things. It hurts magic and the mechanical workings of a trick are just a small percentage of a hard work whose aim is to create wonder.
